('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1012','faith','feθ','feɪθ','[n] 信任，信仰','People have lost faith in the government.  人们已失去了对政府的信心。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1013','upset','ʌp''sɛt','ʌp''set','[v&n] 倾覆，打乱','The chemicals upset the balance of the environment.  这些化学品破坏了环境的平衡。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1014','sabotage',',sæbə''tɑʒ','''sæbətɑːʒ','[n] 故意毁坏，故意破坏，阴谋','The terrorists were planning acts of sabotage to destabilize the country.  恐怖分子在策划破坏国家安定的行动。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1015','slice','slaɪs','slaɪs','[n] 片，部分; [v] 切片','pizza slices  比萨块'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1016','fantasy','''fæntəsi','''fæntəsɪ; -zɪ','[n] 幻想，怪念头','I used to have fantasies about living in Paris with an artist.  我过去常幻想着在巴黎与一位艺术家同住。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1017','expire','ɪk''spaɪɚ','ɪk''spaɪə; ek-','[v] 满期，到期','My passport expires next week.  我的护照下周就到期了。'),
