('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1448','infect','ɪn''fɛkt','ɪn''fekt','[v] 传染，受影响，受感染','People with the virus may feel perfectly well, but they can still infect others.  带有这种病毒的人可能毫无症状，却仍可能传染他人。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1449','symmetry','''sɪmətri','''sɪmɪtrɪ','[n] 对称；匀称','...the incredible beauty and symmetry of a snowflake.  …雪花令人难以置信的美丽和对称。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1450','significant','sɪɡ''nɪfɪkənt','sɪg''nɪfɪk(ə)nt','[adj] 意义深长的；重要的','His most significant political achievement was the abolition of the death penalty.  他政治上最重大的成就是废除了死刑。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1451','currency','ˈkɜrənsi','''kʌr(ə)nsɪ','[n] 通用，流通，货币','The bank can supply you with foreign currency .  这家银行能为你提供外币。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1452','prelude','''prɛljud','''preljuːd','[n] 序言，序幕','Living together as a prelude to marriage is now considered acceptable in many countries.  婚前同居如今在许多国家都已被接受。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1453','typhoon','taɪ''fʊn','taɪ''fuːn','[n] 台风，强热带风暴','The football match have to stand over next week for the typhoon storm.  由于台风风暴，这场足球赛延期到下个星期举行。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1454','discriminate','dɪ''skrɪmɪnet','dɪ''skrɪmɪneɪt','[v] 区别，区分；岐视','He is incapable of discriminating between a good idea and a terrible one.  他没能力在一个好主意和一个坏主意之间进行区分。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1455','drawback','''drɔbæk','''drɔːbæk','[n] 障碍；不利','It’s a great city – the only drawback is the weather.  这是座很不错的城市，唯一的不足就是天气。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1456','vacant','''vekənt','''veɪk(ə)nt','[adj] 空的；未被占用的；空虚的，无表情的','Only a few apartments were still vacant.  只有几套公寓仍然空着。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1457','track','træk','træk','[n&v] 行迹；踪迹；跟踪','The only evidence of pandas was their tracks in the snow.  有熊猫活动的惟一证据就是它们在雪中的足迹。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1458','culture','''kʌltʃɚ','''kʌltʃə','[n] 人类能力的高度发展，文化，教养，文明','We speak Danish at home so that the boys don’t lose touch with their language and culture.  我们在家说丹麦语，这样男孩子们就不会脱离他们的语言和文化。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1459','excavate','''ɛkskə''vet','''ekskəveɪt','[v] 挖掘，挖出','Schliemann excavated the ancient city of Troy.  谢里曼发掘出特洛伊古城。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1460','fit','fɪt','fɪt','[adj] (病的)发作，痉挛; [v&a] n合适,试穿,安装; [v] "','You must be very fit if you do so much running.  如果你经常这样跑步，身体肯定很健康。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1461','motion','''moʃən','''məʊʃ(ə)n','[n] 运动，动态；手势；眼色，姿势；提议','Newton’s first law of motion  牛顿第一运动定律'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1462','expel','ɪk''spɛl','ɪk''spel; ek-','[v] 驱逐，开除；排出','More than five-thousand high school students have been expelled for cheating.  五千多名中学生因考试作弊而被开除。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1463','allowance','ə''laʊəns','ə''laʊəns','[n] 津贴','Sales staff get a generous mileage allowance or a company car.  销售人员有优厚的里程补贴或者公司提供的专用汽车。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1464','coward','''kaʊɚd','''kaʊəd','[n] 胆怯者，懦夫','Try it. Don’t be such a coward.  试一下，别那么胆小。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1465','germ','dʒɝm','dʒɜːm','[n] 幼芽；起源；微生物','This was the germ of a book.  这是一本书的创作萌芽。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1466','flash','flæʃ','flæʃ','[n&v] 闪光，闪现；简讯，浮华','Lightning flashed overhead.  头顶上电光闪闪。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1467','subtract','səb''trækt','səb''trækt','[v] 减去，扣除','The pupil could add and subtract but hadn''t learned to divide.  这名小学生能做加法和减法，但还没学会做除法。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1468','glitter','''ɡlɪtɚ','''glɪtə','[vi&n] 闪闪发光，闪光','The river glittered in the sunlight.  阳光下河面波光粼粼。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1469','predictable','prɪ''dɪktəbl','prɪ''dɪktəb(ə)l','[adj] 可预言的','The snow had a predictable effect on traffic.  这场雪对交通造成的影响可以预见。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1470','undue',',ʌn''du','ʌn''djuː','[adj] 过分的，过度的','De Gaulle felt that America had undue influence in Europe.  戴高乐感到美国在欧洲影响力过大。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1471','dart','dɑrt','dɑːt','[n] 标，镖; [v] 投掷; [v] 急冲','a poisoned dart  毒镖'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_1472','coincide',',koɪn''saɪd',',kəʊɪn''saɪd','[v] 恰好相合，时间巧合；意见一致','The interests of the US and those of the islanders may not coincide.  美国的利益和这些岛民的利益可能并不一致。'),
