('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3053','install','ɪn''stɔl','ɪnˈstɔ:l','[v] 任命；安装，安置','They’ve installed the new computer network at last.  他们终于安装了新电脑网络。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3054','dilute','daɪ''l(j)ut','daɪ''l(j)uːt; dɪ-','[v] 使变淡，稀释; [adj] 稀释的','diluted fruit juice  稀释的果汁'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3055','storey','''stɔri','''stɔːrɪ','[n] 房屋的一层','A staircase leads to the upper storey .  有一段楼梯通往上面一层。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3056','odds','ɑdz','ɒdz','[n] 可能，机会','(= it is likely ) that he will commit the same crime again.  他可能还会犯同样的罪行。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3057','swirl','swɝl','swɜːl','[vt&vi] 打旋，旋动','The river had become a swirling torrent.  河水变成了翻滚的洪流。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3058','reassure',',riə''ʃʊr','riːə''ʃʊə','[v] 使放心，使消除疑虑','Teachers reassured anxious parents.  老师们安慰焦急的父母。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3059','casualty','''kæʒuəlti','''kæʒjʊəltɪ; -zj-','[n] 伤亡人员','We have had our first casualty. One runner has dropped out with cramp.  我们有了第一位伤员，有一位队员因腿部痉挛退出了。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3060','match','mætʃ','mætʃ','[n] 火柴；比赛；对手；婚姻;相称v相当,相配','It’s our last match of the season.  这是我们本赛季最后一场比赛。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3061','decade','''dɛked','''dekeɪd; dɪ''keɪd','[n] 十年','...the last decade of the nineteenth century.  …19世纪的最后10年。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3062','exceed','ɪk''sid','ɪk''siːd; ek-','[v] 比大，超出','Working hours must not exceed 42 hours a week.  工作时间每周不得超过42小时。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3063','tutor','''tʊtɚ','''tjuːtə','[n] 私人教师；[英]大学导师','The children were educated at home by a succession of tutors.  这些孩子在家接受教育，连续请过几任家庭教师。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3064','proximity','prɑk''sɪməti','prɒk''sɪmɪtɪ','[n] 最近，接近','Here the rich and the poor live in close proximity (= very near to each other ) .  在这里，富人和穷人比邻而居。'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3065','cosmopolitan','''kɑzmə''pɑlətn',',kɒzmə''pɒlɪt(ə)n','[adj] 全世界的，世界主义的','a vibrant, cosmopolitan city  一个充满活力的国际性都市'),
('IELTSluan_2','IELTSluan_2_3066','Christian','''krɪstʃən','''krɪstɪən; -tʃ(ə)n','[a&n] 基督教的；基督教徒','He was a devout Christian.  他曾是一个虔诚的基督教徒。'),
