('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_581','bugle','''bjuɡl','''bju:ɡl','[n] 冲锋号','I had been seeing myself on stage, with a war bugle blowing and bullets whizzing by and here I was, a soldier crouching in his trench and ready for a bayonet charge, to take my fate by its throat.  我曾觉得自己是这样的，当军号响起，子弹就在耳旁飞过，而我就在那里，一个士兵蜷伏在战壕中并准备用刺刀冲锋，来掌握我的命运之喉。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_582','revolution','''rɛvə''lʊʃən','ˌrevəˈlu:ʃn','[n] 革命','the French Revolution of 1789  1789年法国大革命'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_583','proportion','prə''pɔrʃən','prəˈpɔ:ʃn','[n] 比例','The proportion of women in the profession had risen to 17.3%.  从事那个职业的女性比例已经增长到17.3%。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_584','convince','kən''vɪns','kənˈvɪns','[v] 使信服,使相信','Her arguments didn’t convince everyone, but changes were made.  她的论点不能说服每个人，但还是引起了一些变化。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_585','ribbon','''rɪbən','ˈrɪbən','[n] 缎带，丝带','little girls with ribbons in their hair  头发上系着丝带的小姑娘们'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_586','chase','','tʃeɪs','[v] 追逐','The dogs saw him running and chased him.  那些狗看到他在跑就追他。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_587','unconscious','ʌn''kɑnʃəs','ʌnˈkɒnʃəs','[adj] 无意识的','Doreen appeared to be unconscious of the amusement she had caused.  多琳似乎并未意识到她把大家逗乐了。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_588','gutter','''gʌtɚ','ˈgʌtə(r)','[n] （路边）排水沟','The gutters were blocked and overflowing.  排水沟堵住了，水都溢出来了。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_589','integral','''ɪntɪɡrəl','ˈɪntɪgrəl','[adj] 构成整体所必需的','Rituals, celebrations, and festivals form an integral part of every human society.  仪式、庆典和节日是每个人类社会不可缺少的组成部分。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_590','contemporary','kən''tɛmpərɛri','kənˈtemprəri','[adj] 当代的；同时代的','She writes a lot of contemporary music for people like Whitney Houston.  她为惠特尼·休斯敦等人创作大量当代音乐作品。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_591','archaeologist',',ɑrkɪ''ɑlədʒɪst','ˌɑ:kiˈɒlədʒɪst','[n] 考古学家','In fact, she was an archaeologist.  其实她是一个考古学家。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_592','indulgent','ɪn''dʌldʒənt','ɪnˈdʌldʒənt','[adj] 放纵的，纵容的','toys bought by their indulgent grandparents  溺爱孩子的(外)祖父母买的玩具'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_593','humanitarian','hju,mænɪ''tɛrɪən','hju:,mæni''tεəriən','[n] 人道主义者','And on each of those issues we have said that we would consider that and, in fact, have provided some humanitarian support.  对于每一件这样的事情，我们都说过，我们将会对此进行考虑，事实上，我们向他们提供了人道主义援助。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_594','promulgate','''prɑmlɡet','ˈprɒmlgeɪt','[v] 颁布，公布','A new constitution was promulgated last month.  上个月颁布了一部新宪法。'),
('Level4luan_1','Level4luan_1_595','essence','''ɛsns','ˈesns','[n] 本质，实质','In essence his message was very simple.  实质上他想表达的意思很简单。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_1','younger','''jʌŋɡɚ','''jʌŋɡə','更年轻的','The younger people might not like the idea.  年轻一些的人可能不喜欢这个主意。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_2','older','oldə','''əʊldə','更年长的','I like the older one.This one.  我喜欢年纪大点儿的这个。这个。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_3','taller','''tɔlɚ','''tɔ:lə(r)','更高的','Like you, a bit, but smarter, taller and better looking.  就像你，有一点点，但是更聪明、更高、更好看。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_4','shorter','','','更矮的','The idea is to finish a job in a shorter time as measured by an external clock, even if at the cost of more hardware and programming complexity.  其思想是按照外部时钟的步调在更短的时间内完成一项工作，即便要以更复杂的硬件和编程为代价也在所不惜。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_5','longer','''lɔŋɡɚ','''lɒŋɡə','更长的','The article was abstracted from a longer new book.  这篇文章是从一本较长的新书中摘选出来的。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_6','thinner','''θɪnɚ','''θɪnə','更瘦的','As she looked up to see who I meant — though already knowing, probably, from my tone — suddenly he looked at her, the thinner one, the boyish one, the youngest, perhaps.  当她抬头看向我所指的人时——也许从我的声音里就已经听出来了——忽然，他看着她，那个最瘦的，最孩子气的，也许是最年轻的男孩。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_7','heavier','''hɛvɪɚðən''ɛr','''hevɪə','更重的','Just as in the sun, the chain reaction in the second stage fuses the hydrogen atoms into heavier helium atoms and releases vast amounts of energy in the process.  正如在太阳上所进行的反应一样，第二阶段连锁反应将氢原子聚合成较重的氦原子并在这一过程中释放出巨大的能量。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_8','bigger','bɪgə(r)','bɪgə(r)','更大的','That uncertain thing was swelled bigger.  那个不知叫什么的东西膨胀得更大了。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_9','smaller','smɔlər','smɔ:lə(r)','更小的','Inside the reactor the large molecules are cracked into smaller molecules.  在反应堆内部大的分子被裂解为较小的分子。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_10','stronger','strɔ:ŋɡər','strɒŋgə(r)','更强壮的','Then you must be stronger than us.  那么你一定比我们强壮。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_11','dinosaur','ˈdaɪnəˌsɔr','''daɪnəsɔː','恐龙','How then would this dinosaur have moved?  那么这种恐龙要如何移动呢？'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_12','hall','hɔl','hɔːl','大厅','a huge tiled entrance hall  铺着地砖的大门厅'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_13','metre','ˈmitɚ','''mi:tə(r)','米','Let me congratulate you on your winning first place in the 100 metre dash.  祝贺你获得百米赛跑第一名。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_14','meter','mitɚ','ˈmi:tə(r)','米','He came in third in the hundred-meter dash.  在百米竞赛中他跑了第三名。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_15','than','ðæn','ðæn; ð(ə)n','比','Natalie was prettier than her sister.  纳塔莉比她姐姐漂亮。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_16','both','boθ','bəʊθ','两个都','Both Helen’s parents are doctors.  海伦的父母都是医生。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_17','kilogram','''kɪləɡræm','ˈkɪləɡræm','千克','For example, the kilogram scale allows you to assign a number to an object indicating its weight based upon standardized displacements of measuring instruments.  例如，千克尺度允许您给一个物体分配数字，根据测量仪器的标准化的偏移量指示该物体的重量。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_18','countryside','''kʌntrɪsaɪd','''kʌntrɪsaɪd','乡村','The house had lovely views over open countryside .  这房子望出去是开阔的乡村美景。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_19','lower','''loɚ','''ləʊə','更低地','Don''t lower yourself, don''t be the way they are.  不要贬低自己的身份，别像他们那样。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_20','shadow','''ʃædo','''ʃædəʊ','影子','the long dark shadow of an old oak tree  一棵老橡树长长的影子'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_21','smarter','','''smɑ:tə','更聪明的','If he is smarter than you ,he is great,but you are fool.  如果他比你聪明，他就是有智慧，而你是傻瓜。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_22','become','bɪ''kʌm','bɪ''kʌm','变成','The weather became warmer.  天气变暖和了。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_23','cleaned','klind','kliːnd','打扫','Mary cooked and cleaned for them.  玛丽为他们做饭、打扫卫生。'),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_24','stayed','','','待',''),
('PEPXiaoXue6_2','PEPXiaoXue6_2_25','washed','wɔʃt','wɔʃt','洗','We did odd jobs like farm work and washing dishes.  我们做了一些诸如干农活儿和洗盘子之类的零活儿。'),
